  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Protection, Health, and Resilience of Refugees and host communities in Cox&#x2019;s Bazar, Bangladesh (language: English)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Now in its sixth year, the Rohingya crisis is a protracted crisis. The stateless Rohingyas are currently residing in extremely overcrowded camps, no freedom of movement out of camps, restricted access to rights and specific protection needs which contribute to cyclical denial of identity, persecution, and displacement. The project will provide a comprehensive set of activities which will be executed through a complementing and integrated approach using protection mechanisms, improve basic rights, access to legal assistance, housing, land, and property (HLP) and access to essential services such as education, health care and tailored assistance to people with disabilities in Cox&apos;s Bazar and Bhasan Char.</narrative>
  </description>
